  "image_sha256": "60c48e8ce5fd289f6aa7b80cfd5a99db1adf9a0603e6162c1fb5b4dcf1a7e15d",
  "old_problem": "In the figure below, $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles. If $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD$ and $m \\angle COB = 50^\\circ$, find $m \\angle AOD$.\n\n![](images/60/60c48e8ce5fd289f6aa7b80cfd5a99db1adf9a0603e6162c1fb5b4dcf1a7e15d.png)",
  "current_problem": "In the figure below, $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles. If $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD$ and $m \\angle COB = 50^\\circ,$ find $m \\angle AOD.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14186058/assets/60c48e8ce5fd289f6aa7b80cfd5a99db1adf9a0603e6162c1fb5b4dcf1a7e15d.png)",
  "old_solution": "Since $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠AOC + m∠COB &= 90^{∘} \\\\\nm∠AOC + 50^{∘} &= 90^{∘} \\\\\nm∠AOC &= 40^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD$, we have\n\n$$\nm \\angle BOD = m \\angle AOC=40^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠AOD &= m∠AOC + m∠COB + m∠BOD \\\\\n&= 40^{∘} + 50^{∘} + 40^{∘} \\\\\n&= 130^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "current_solution": "Since $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC+m∠COB & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOC+{50}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOC & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD,$ we have\n\n$$\nm \\angle BOD = m \\angle AOC=40^\\circ .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOD & =m∠AOC+m∠COB+m∠BOD \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}+{50}^{∘}+{40}^{∘} \\\\  & ={130}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
