  "reasoning": "The source example is the same complementary-angle problem, not a new item: both use AOC and COB complementary, AOC congruent to BOD, COB=50 degrees, and ask for AOD. Both derive AOC=BOD=40 degrees and AOD=130 degrees. The diagram bytes have exactly the same SHA-256. Math Academy renamed the skill from Using a Diagram and Properties of Complementary Angles to Find an Unknown Angle to Solving Multi-Step Problems Involving Complementary Angles. Its current reference pool assigns q-27363 to source example 18993; that same question is already owned by the existing KP. Reuse the KP and canonical UUIDs and retain the existing question pool."
